WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.682
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.608 --> 00:00:09.334
- [Sarah] Do I mend my broken relationship

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:11.251
with my abusive mother?

00:00:14.224 --> 00:00:15.057
Yes or no?

00:00:16.435 --> 00:00:19.185
(dynamic music)

00:00:32.004 --> 00:00:33.324
- I think family's very important.

00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:35.584
If you can at least try to have some kind

00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:37.539
of communication between
you and your mother

00:00:37.539 --> 00:00:39.203
I think that's a very important thing.

00:00:39.203 --> 00:00:41.667
- I think it's a very
subjective situation though,

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.535
because when you have an
abusive person in your life

00:00:44.535 --> 00:00:46.987
it's really, really hard
to keep amends with them.

00:00:46.987 --> 00:00:51.141
So I think it does depend
too, have you tried before?

00:00:51.141 --> 00:00:52.954
What is the situation like?

00:00:52.954 --> 00:00:53.787
Yeah.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.463
- [Sarah] My mom has
terminal brain cancer.

00:00:58.463 --> 00:01:01.665
I feel like I'm running out of time.

00:01:01.665 --> 00:01:03.782
- [Director] If that
changed your decision,

00:01:03.782 --> 00:01:06.865
you guys are welcome to switch sides.

00:01:08.686 --> 00:01:10.404
- [Jury Member] There we go.

00:01:10.404 --> 00:01:12.237
- [Jury Member] Sorry.

00:01:13.592 --> 00:01:15.481
- I just wouldn't want you to regret.

00:01:15.481 --> 00:01:17.348
I've had the same type of thought,

00:01:17.348 --> 00:01:19.302
should I cut someone outta my life?

00:01:19.302 --> 00:01:21.549
But then, I don't wanna hold this anger

00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:25.428
and resentment for this person,
and die with this feeling.

00:01:25.428 --> 00:01:26.904
- I actually did experience that.

00:01:26.904 --> 00:01:28.643
My mother did pass of cancer

00:01:28.643 --> 00:01:29.873
and I did not have a good relationship

00:01:29.873 --> 00:01:31.626
with her the majority of my life.

00:01:31.626 --> 00:01:33.072
I did not get her very long,

00:01:33.072 --> 00:01:35.742
but at least the last few
years that we did have

00:01:35.742 --> 00:01:37.436
we were able to have open conversations,

00:01:37.436 --> 00:01:40.157
and me hear her perspective
for the first time ever.

00:01:40.157 --> 00:01:41.985
And it gave me a very
different view on things,

00:01:41.985 --> 00:01:44.815
because as parents, I am a mother of five,

00:01:44.815 --> 00:01:47.437
we do the best we can with
what we have at the moment.

00:01:47.437 --> 00:01:50.229
To know I loved her, I knew she loved me,

00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:52.447
completely changed everything
when she did pass on,

00:01:52.447 --> 00:01:54.364
which was 10 years ago.

00:01:55.696 --> 00:01:58.421
- I was raised in a
cult-like religious community

00:01:58.421 --> 00:02:00.383
where my abuse occurred.

00:02:00.383 --> 00:02:02.485
Due to my mother's religious conditioning,

00:02:02.485 --> 00:02:05.235
she swept my abuse under the rug.

00:02:06.254 --> 00:02:07.912
- [Director] You guys have
another chance to switch sides

00:02:07.912 --> 00:02:09.995
if you feel compelled to.

00:02:18.269 --> 00:02:19.779
- It's difficult being in a cult,

00:02:19.779 --> 00:02:21.456
just thinking of being brainwashed.

00:02:21.456 --> 00:02:23.789
And that could've affected her mom.

00:02:23.789 --> 00:02:25.763
And maybe the cult was encouraging

00:02:25.763 --> 00:02:28.001
to act like it didn't happen.

00:02:28.001 --> 00:02:31.501
- When parents show stress around a child,

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.211
that kid will pick up on the stress.

00:02:34.211 --> 00:02:36.793
And maybe this was her attempt to

00:02:36.793 --> 00:02:38.751
maybe make it not hurt as bad.

00:02:38.751 --> 00:02:40.803
And it's not the right thing to do,

00:02:40.803 --> 00:02:44.597
but maybe this was kind of
her way of dealing with it.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.202
- I would just like to
add though, attempting to

00:02:47.202 --> 00:02:49.529
mend the relationship does
not excuse the behavior.

00:02:49.529 --> 00:02:51.347
- Yes.
- Definitely.

00:02:51.347 --> 00:02:52.180
- [Jury Member] Right.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:53.969
- It's more about
understanding the context

00:02:53.969 --> 00:02:55.552
and trying to seek closure for yourself.

00:02:55.552 --> 00:02:57.635
- [Jury Member] Exactly.

00:02:59.591 --> 00:03:03.508
- A pastor of my church
coerced and groomed me.

00:03:06.026 --> 00:03:08.553
He was married, I babysat his children.

00:03:08.553 --> 00:03:12.546
My abuse caused me to lose my community.

00:03:12.546 --> 00:03:14.884
When I had gotten strong enough

00:03:14.884 --> 00:03:19.001
to potentially try and bring it to light

00:03:19.001 --> 00:03:22.499
my mom did have evidence of the abuse.

00:03:22.499 --> 00:03:24.832
And she chose to destroy it.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:35.288
- How many times have you tried
to mend this relationship?

00:03:35.288 --> 00:03:37.200
- Probably for my whole life.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.899
My last contact with her was in April.

00:03:40.899 --> 00:03:43.649
I flew states away to be with her

00:03:44.841 --> 00:03:47.763
and she walked out of a room I was in.

00:03:47.763 --> 00:03:50.307
And that was how we said goodbye that day.

00:03:50.307 --> 00:03:52.539
I lived a pretty gaslit existence

00:03:52.539 --> 00:03:56.181
and so I wasn't always aware
of the abuse I lived in.

00:03:56.181 --> 00:03:59.118
It's only been the last decade or so

00:03:59.118 --> 00:04:02.469
that I have learned about myself,

00:04:02.469 --> 00:04:04.886
and what is right and normal.

00:04:08.739 --> 00:04:10.550
Sorry.
- It's okay.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:14.235
- You do not have to apologize
for being a human being.

00:04:14.235 --> 00:04:17.879
- For your personal peace, and
for you to find forgiveness,

00:04:17.879 --> 00:04:19.892
do you think that that requires

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.605
a mended relationship with your mom?

00:04:22.605 --> 00:04:24.132
- At the time of her diagnosis,

00:04:24.132 --> 00:04:27.913
she had a 1% chance to
live the next five years.

00:04:27.913 --> 00:04:29.496
It's been one year.

00:04:31.042 --> 00:04:32.725
With her diagnosis, it's clear to me

00:04:32.725 --> 00:04:35.725
that she's willing to die with this.

00:04:36.824 --> 00:04:39.241
And that is so extreme to me.

00:04:40.086 --> 00:04:41.567
She has asked me questions like,

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:43.310
well, think of his children.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:45.622
She's befriended his ex-wife,

00:04:45.622 --> 00:04:49.137
who is the wife he was married
to when all of this happened.

00:04:49.137 --> 00:04:50.459
And it feels really extreme.

00:04:50.459 --> 00:04:55.247
It feels bad to know that
my mother is suffering

00:04:55.247 --> 00:04:58.829
and to not be able to comfort
her in the way that I wish.

00:04:58.829 --> 00:05:01.077
But in order to do that,
it really feels like

00:05:01.077 --> 00:05:03.077
I'm letting myself down.

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:07.399
And I'm the only one that's
going to stand up for myself.

00:05:07.399 --> 00:05:09.602
There's nobody else.

00:05:09.602 --> 00:05:14.426
And so to appease her death so
she can have a peaceful death

00:05:14.426 --> 00:05:18.176
when my life has been
so tumultuous, I can't.

00:05:23.637 --> 00:05:25.721
- This is tough.
- Yeah, I understand.

00:05:25.721 --> 00:05:26.725
- [Jury Member] It's, this is tough.

00:05:26.725 --> 00:05:30.600
- Your mother doesn't
deserve to have that peace.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.149
And I feel like mending that relationship

00:05:32.149 --> 00:05:33.799
is gonna give her peace,

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:34.850
and you're not gonna have that

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.309
because you've had a traumatic life.

00:05:37.309 --> 00:05:38.818
- I totally understand the boundaries.

00:05:38.818 --> 00:05:40.701
I agree with all of your points.

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:41.909
But this is your mother.

00:05:41.909 --> 00:05:43.371
Things don't just go away over time.

00:05:43.371 --> 00:05:44.475
I think that's the biggest lie.

00:05:44.475 --> 00:05:45.345
Time heals things.

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.298
No, it does not.

00:05:46.298 --> 00:05:48.623
You addressing your things heals things.

00:05:48.623 --> 00:05:50.687
And so you have an opportunity to do that.

00:05:50.687 --> 00:05:52.633
And she doesn't have much time left to.

00:05:52.633 --> 00:05:54.445
- Sorry to kind of
counteract the whole thing

00:05:54.445 --> 00:05:55.671
where it's like, it's your mom.

00:05:55.671 --> 00:05:57.530
Blood only goes so far.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:00.287
And her being blood related to you

00:06:00.287 --> 00:06:03.416
doesn't excuse everything that she's done.

00:06:03.416 --> 00:06:04.703
- I kind of disagree a little bit.

00:06:04.703 --> 00:06:07.522
I think it definitely doesn't excuse.

00:06:07.522 --> 00:06:10.498
If she doesn't wanna take
accountability, that's on her.

00:06:10.498 --> 00:06:12.424
That's not your problem anymore.

00:06:12.424 --> 00:06:14.872
But for your own sake, and
for your own peace of mind,

00:06:14.872 --> 00:06:15.753
I think it's really important

00:06:15.753 --> 00:06:17.870
that you really give it your all,

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.478
especially in this crucial
time that you have.

00:06:20.478 --> 00:06:21.475
- I was wondering, what do you need

00:06:21.475 --> 00:06:24.808
in this moment to feel safe and secure?

00:06:28.919 --> 00:06:30.169
- I don't know.

00:06:31.237 --> 00:06:33.237
I would like validation.

00:06:35.437 --> 00:06:38.094
I would like to feel loved.

00:06:38.094 --> 00:06:41.511
I would like to feel a part of something.

00:06:42.404 --> 00:06:44.943
- Do you currently have a support system?

00:06:44.943 --> 00:06:48.588
And if so, what does
that look like for you?

00:06:48.588 --> 00:06:50.637
- That's been really hard.

00:06:50.637 --> 00:06:53.625
That's been a trending struggle in my life

00:06:53.625 --> 00:06:56.256
because I feel like I've carried around

00:06:56.256 --> 00:06:58.256
feeling like an outcast.

00:06:59.159 --> 00:07:02.072
I feel like I've been chosen over.

00:07:02.072 --> 00:07:06.822
And that I am not worth even
my mother's care or concern.

00:07:12.975 --> 00:07:16.392
So finding community with that on my back

00:07:18.042 --> 00:07:20.125
has been a very big deal.

00:07:23.068 --> 00:07:27.485
I do have a spouse, and I
do have a six year old son,

00:07:29.095 --> 00:07:33.062
and they're the best things in my life.

00:07:33.062 --> 00:07:36.062
(suspenseful music)

00:07:40.574 --> 00:07:42.034
- [Chelsy] It just seems
like it's at a point

00:07:42.034 --> 00:07:43.465
where she's tried everything.

00:07:43.465 --> 00:07:44.831
- [Jennifer] Her mother must have value,

00:07:44.831 --> 00:07:46.379
because she wouldn't be doing all this.

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:49.865
- [Chelsy] I think she's
actually found her peace.

00:07:49.865 --> 00:07:51.496
If her mom wasn't sick, I
don't think she would be

00:07:51.496 --> 00:07:52.757
in this situation right now.

00:07:52.757 --> 00:07:55.858
The diagnosis brought up
a lot of pent-up anger

00:07:55.858 --> 00:07:58.236
inside of her that she
now wants to put out.

00:07:58.236 --> 00:08:00.392
- [Joseph] If her mother
dies, and looks back and says,

00:08:00.392 --> 00:08:02.410
I wish I did this, I wish I did that.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.847
I think that's gonna end
up eating her even worse.

00:08:04.847 --> 00:08:07.201
- [Daniel] The ground zero
should be, what does she want?

00:08:07.201 --> 00:08:08.034
- Yeah.
- Exactly.

00:08:08.034 --> 00:08:08.867
What does she want?

00:08:08.867 --> 00:08:10.450
What does she need?

00:08:14.124 --> 00:08:17.693
- We all agree that it is
better to regret doing something

00:08:17.693 --> 00:08:19.267
than not doing something.

00:08:19.267 --> 00:08:20.100
You never know what it's like

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.589
when someone's on their deathbed.

00:08:21.589 --> 00:08:23.928
And so we just feel like
keeping the door open

00:08:23.928 --> 00:08:26.746
is better than keeping the door closed.

00:08:26.746 --> 00:08:29.088
- We were listening to what
you stated that you wanted.

00:08:29.088 --> 00:08:31.972
You wanted to feel loved
and you wanted validation.

00:08:31.972 --> 00:08:33.364
You can achieve those things

00:08:33.364 --> 00:08:37.020
without mending the relationship,
through support systems,

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:39.264
finding therapy, finding a community.

00:08:39.264 --> 00:08:41.489
You have the love from
your family on your side.

00:08:41.489 --> 00:08:45.822
So for that reason, we said,
you should not mend it.

00:08:48.274 --> 00:08:51.577
- [Director] Have you made your decision?

00:08:51.577 --> 00:08:52.744
- [Sarah] Yes.

00:09:07.602 --> 00:09:09.275
Like you guys said, I can offer myself

00:09:09.275 --> 00:09:11.997
the things that I need moving forward.

00:09:11.997 --> 00:09:16.282
And mending the relationship
takes a lot of energy

00:09:16.282 --> 00:09:17.593
and takes me back to a lot of places

00:09:17.593 --> 00:09:19.953
that I've already moved through.

00:09:19.953 --> 00:09:22.318
Both boxes really suck for me.

00:09:22.318 --> 00:09:26.151
And I like the possibilities
in this box more.

00:09:27.445 --> 00:09:30.195
(dynamic music)

00:09:31.661 --> 00:09:33.007
On the show, that was the first time

00:09:33.007 --> 00:09:34.625
I've ever talked about it.

00:09:34.625 --> 00:09:37.952
I came away feeling like maybe
I had a powerless attitude

00:09:37.952 --> 00:09:41.973
towards it, and it didn't
have to be that way.

00:09:41.973 --> 00:09:43.618
I have spoken to pretty much

00:09:43.618 --> 00:09:46.978
everyone now about this situation.

00:09:46.978 --> 00:09:50.724
So I decided to get in
contact with law enforcement

00:09:50.724 --> 00:09:52.887
and have a conversation with a detective

00:09:52.887 --> 00:09:55.268
just going over what happened to me.

00:09:55.268 --> 00:09:56.290
- [Director] Was there any part of you

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:59.455
that wanted to reach out to your mom

00:09:59.455 --> 00:10:01.740
when you did reach out to law enforcement?

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.398
- [Sarah] It's a lot harder to do

00:10:03.398 --> 00:10:05.562
when interacting in real time.

00:10:05.562 --> 00:10:09.667
I find myself more thinking
of writing her letters

00:10:09.667 --> 00:10:11.973
to just know that I'm expressing myself.

00:10:11.973 --> 00:10:14.932
And so I'm hoping that will serve

00:10:14.932 --> 00:10:17.432
for some kind of olive branch.

00:10:18.356 --> 00:10:21.775
Since opening up that
dialogue with the jury

00:10:21.775 --> 00:10:24.879
I have found myself much more open

00:10:24.879 --> 00:10:27.129
to finding a middle ground.

00:10:31.268 --> 00:10:36.268
♪ I love, I love, I love, I love
you like la, la, la, la, la ♪

00:10:38.356 --> 00:10:42.247
♪ I love you like la, la, la, la, la, la ♪

00:10:42.247 --> 00:10:43.769
♪ I love, I love, I love you ♪

